# Environment variable names only

Copy to `.env.local` for local development. **Never commit real values.**  
Fabricated data only in local and staging.  
`NODE_ENV` is managed by Next.js / Vercel — do not set it here.

## App

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
```

## Supabase

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Exception-only server credential. Never expose to the browser or routine Trigger.dev workers.
# Authorized holders (Phase 1+): narrowly documented admin/migration scripts or emergency
# repair jobs only — never the default worker path (see docs/phase-0/WORKER_AUTHORIZATION.md).
# Prefer Pattern C (signed automation identity → internal domain API).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional direct DB URL for migrations tooling only — not for Trigger.dev workers by default
SUPABASE_DB_URL=
```

## Auth allowlist

```bash
# Comma-separated AITHERAS emails approved to sign in
AUTH_ALLOWLIST_EMAILS=
```

## Durable jobs (Trigger.dev recommended)

```bash
# Worker receives TRIGGER_* secrets and a signed automation credential for Pattern C —
# not SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY by default.
TRIGGER_SECRET_KEY=
TRIGGER_PROJECT_ID=
HRIS_AUTOMATION_CLIENT_ID=
HRIS_AUTOMATION_CLIENT_SECRET=
```

## Optional — Inngest alternative

```bash
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=
```

## Google OAuth (via Supabase provider / Google Cloud)

```bash
# Configured primarily in Supabase + Google Cloud Console; document client IDs out of band
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
```

## Integration placeholders (Phase 0B+ — server only)

```bash
JAZZHR_API_KEY=
# OPENAI — not required for Phase 0; provision before AI enablement
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_PROJECT_ID=
```

## Feature flags / ops

```bash
# Defaults to true (AI blocked). Set false only when OpenAI is provisioned and approved.
AI_GLOBAL_KILL_SWITCH=true
```
